From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Chris Bongaarts <cab@bongalow.net>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 02:28:14 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] 10217: Decompiler: label switch cases with indexes, not byte
 offsets, when index scaled by a left shift

Decompiler: label switches by the index when it is scaled by
 a left shift

JumpBasic::findUnnormalized walks back from the normalized switch
variable through INT_ADD/INT_SUB and INT_ZEXT/INT_SEXT, but not through
INT_LEFT, even though it receives maxleftright (JumpTable::maxleftright,
"Maximum shifts to normalize") and OpBehaviorIntLeft::recoverInputBinary
already reverses a shift for backup2Switch. When the bounded value is
the scaled index (common on 8-bit CPUs: ASL A; TAY; LDA table,Y), the
cases were labelled with byte offsets 0,2,4,... instead of the index
0,1,2,...

Add a CPUI_INT_LEFT case: a shift by a constant in slot 0, limited by
maxleftright and smaller than the output width, makes the shifted input
the switch variable. The labels are then recovered through the existing
recoverInputBinary.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01NvtBaQBU5K9LiCeqXgAhG3
---
 .../Decompiler/src/decompile/cpp/jumptable.cc         | 11 +++++++++++
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+)

diff --git a/Ghidra/Features/Decompiler/src/decompile/cpp/jumptable.cc b/Ghidra/Features/Decompiler/src/decompile/cpp/jumptable.cc
index d8bfce88f8..28d39504f6 100644
--- a/Ghidra/Features/Decompiler/src/decompile/cpp/jumptable.cc
+++ b/Ghidra/Features/Decompiler/src/decompile/cpp/jumptable.cc
@@ -1592,6 +1592,7 @@ void JumpBasic::findUnnormalized(uint4 maxaddsub,uint4 maxleftright,uint4 maxext
   markModel(true);
 
   int4 countaddsub=0;
+  int4 countleftright=0;
   int4 countext=0;
   PcodeOp *normop = (PcodeOp *)0;
   while(i<pathMeld.numCommonVarnode()) {
@@ -1610,6 +1611,16 @@ void JumpBasic::findUnnormalized(uint4 maxaddsub,uint4 maxleftright,uint4 maxext
       if (!normop->getIn(1-j)->isConstant()) break;
       switchvn = testvn;
       break;
+    case CPUI_INT_LEFT:
+      // An index scaled by a shift (i << c, e.g. a word table indexed by i*2) is labeled
+      // by i, not by the byte offset.  backup2Switch reverses it through
+      // OpBehaviorIntLeft::recoverInputBinary.
+      countleftright += 1;
+      if (countleftright > maxleftright) break;
+      if (j != 0 || !normop->getIn(1)->isConstant()) break;
+      if (normop->getIn(1)->getOffset() >= 8*normop->getOut()->getSize()) break;
+      switchvn = testvn;
+      break;
     case CPUI_INT_ZEXT:
     case CPUI_INT_SEXT:
       countext += 1;
